  "term": "infertility",
  "definition": "Infertility is a condition affecting many individuals and couples that can have major social and health effects. In psychology and counselling contexts, it is relevant because it is often linked with stigma, financial strain, physical and mental health problems, and emotional difficulties such as anxiety, depression, and stress within married life.",
